WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.413 --> 00:00:17.574
spent the next day giving away more gold.

2
00:00:19.716 --> 00:00:22.137
He gave gold to farmers whose crops had failed.

3
00:00:23.719 --> 00:00:26.200
He gave some to a woman who fed stray cats.

4
00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:31.324
"I need to rest for a little while," he thought.

5
00:00:33.632 --> 00:00:34.753
He landed on a tree.

6
00:00:36.174 --> 00:00:37.875
Below, two men were talking.

7
00:00:37.895 --> 00:00:42.238
"Yes," one said.

8
00:00:42.258 --> 00:00:46.621
"A swallow dropped a piece of gold right at my feet."

9
00:00:46.901 --> 00:00:51.985
"It happened to me too," his friend said.

10
00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:54.747
A woman walked by.

11
00:00:54.767 --> 00:00:58.169
"Are you talking about the bird with the gold?"

12
00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:01.652
When they nodded, she smiled.

13
00:01:02.868 --> 00:01:04.629
"The swallow visited me too.

14
00:01:05.990 --> 00:01:09.512
I bought food, candles, and wood for the fireplace."

15
00:01:12.353 --> 00:01:15.515
More people gathered, sharing stories about the bird.

16
00:01:17.036 --> 00:01:18.877
Then one man frowned.

17
00:01:18.897 --> 00:01:22.259
"That bird ruined our statue!"

18
00:01:26.241 --> 00:01:28.763
just a statue," someone said.

19
00:01:28.783 --> 00:01:31.144
"Which is more important?

20
00:01:32.368 --> 00:01:35.450
A beautiful statue or the people of this town?"

21
00:01:37.231 --> 00:01:38.372
The man grumbled again.

22
00:01:38.912 --> 00:01:39.772
But then he shrugged.

23
00:01:39.792 --> 00:01:42.434
"I suppose you're right.

24
00:01:43.695 --> 00:01:46.376
It's better for people to have food and shelter."

25
00:01:49.478 --> 00:01:52.120
Swallow flew off to tell the statue what he heard.

26
00:01:57.383 --> 00:01:58.483
are very grateful!"

27
00:01:58.883 --> 00:01:59.564
Swallow said.

28
00:02:01.076 --> 00:02:04.497
"I don't know how to thank you," the statue said.

29
00:02:04.517 --> 00:02:08.659
"You don't have to," Swallow said.

30
00:02:08.679 --> 00:02:11.660
"Helping people brings me joy.

31
00:02:14.121 --> 00:02:16.322
And I've learned something new about beauty.

32
00:02:17.503 --> 00:02:20.224
But Prince, you have one last piece of gold.

33
00:02:24.245 --> 00:02:25.306
Do you want to keep it?"

34
00:02:26.306 --> 00:02:27.907
"No," the statue said.

35
00:02:27.927 --> 00:02:30.288
"I have a plan.

36
00:02:31.672 --> 00:02:34.173
Can you help me once more before you leave?"

37
00:02:34.193 --> 00:02:36.494
"Of course!

38
00:02:36.874 --> 00:02:37.995
I'll do it in the morning."

39
00:02:41.256 --> 00:02:43.997
That evening the two friends looked out over the town.

40
00:02:44.017 --> 00:02:47.319
"Does the town look different?"

41
00:02:47.739 --> 00:02:48.579
Swallow asked.

42
00:02:48.599 --> 00:02:52.481
"It's brighter," the statue said.

43
00:02:52.501 --> 00:02:55.502
"Candles glow in windows.

44
00:02:57.643 --> 00:03:00.124
Fires burn in hearths, and listen!

45
00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:04.262
People are talking and laughing."

46
00:03:04.282 --> 00:03:08.484
"It's a wonderful sound."

47
00:03:13.728 --> 00:03:18.150
At sunrise the statue told Swallow who should get the last gold piece.

48
00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:20.672
"Why him?"

49
00:03:21.132 --> 00:03:22.753
Swallow asked in surprise.

50
00:03:22.773 --> 00:03:26.696
"You'll see," the statue said.

51
00:03:31.964 --> 00:03:33.585
Swallow flew to a cottage.

52
00:03:34.926 --> 00:03:38.008
Outside he saw firewood, a cow, and chickens.

53
00:03:40.789 --> 00:03:43.491
Inside, a young man sat writing.

54
00:03:46.193 --> 00:03:48.914
Suddenly he sighed and lay down his pen.

55
00:03:48.934 --> 00:03:53.157
"Why do I waste my time?

56
00:03:53.177 --> 00:03:57.559
No one will ever read my stories."

57
00:04:01.716 --> 00:04:03.337
"Oh!" Swallow thought.

58
00:04:03.357 --> 00:04:06.117
"This young man has plenty of food.

59
00:04:08.078 --> 00:04:09.578
But he needs something else."

60
00:04:11.399 --> 00:04:15.460
Whoosh! Swallow swooped in and dropped the gold.

61
00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:18.461
The writer cheered.

62
00:04:22.082 --> 00:04:22.822
a gift!

63
00:04:24.142 --> 00:04:26.323
Now I can publish my stories."

64
00:04:29.084 --> 00:04:30.304
He stared at the gold.

65
00:04:32.393 --> 00:04:35.241
"And maybe I have an idea for a new one."
